# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
# Symptom: BED file uses comma as field delimiter instead of tab; arises from
#   Excel export as CSV or from R write.csv() without specifying sep="\t".
#   All parsers that split on tab will fail to parse the fields.
#   bedtools reports "Unexpected file format. Please use tab-delimited BED".
#   This is distinct from space-separated (space_separated.bed is in corpus)
#   and from comma in blockSizes/blockStarts (those use comma as LIST separator).
chr1,100,200,feature001,0,+
chr1,300,400,feature002,255,-
chr2,1000,2000,feature003,500,+
